            "review_text": "Ben_Chng\nHanoi, Vietnam150 contributions\n0\nSizzling great taste!\nJun 2016 • Friends\nIt is a fastfood table service restaurant from Japan found in many Asian countries. Have eaten it before in both Japan and Singapore so i can say the franchise in Vietnam tastes as good as the other countries. \nThe interesting thing about this place is that every dish is served in a sizzling hot plate where you cook the food yourself. A welcome change to the numerous copy/paste japanese/korean bbq you can find anywhere in Saigon. The price can be slightly more expensive than what you would expect if you are a local, but the quality and quantity justifies that price. And the best thing is it tastes great and the sauces were just heavenly. I usually order their most popular Beef Pepper Rice and if i am in the mood to splurge, i will go for the Ribeye steak. \n\nIt is really popular and have spawn quite a few local copycats that sell cheaper but uses lower quality stuff. I have tried those but the taste is so different and cannot be compared once you have tried the original Pepper Lunch.\n\nStaff are friendly and cheerful. Despite their lack of English skills, they try their best.\n\nLocation wise, you can find them in most of the major shopping malls.\nRead more\nWritten June 5, 2016",
